  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing \u2014 app cannot reach database.\n\n**Root cause: database container detached from network, DNS `db` unresolvable from app.**\n\n* `incidentlab-app-1` and `incidentlab-db-1` both `running` (E1), but app `Up 5 seconds`, db `Up 10 seconds (healthy)` \u2014 both very recently (re)started.\n* App `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n* App logs show both `upload` and `health` failing at `psycopg.connect` with:\n  `psycopg.OperationalError: failed to resolve host 'db': [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution` (E3).\n* App is attached to `[\"incidentlab_default\"]` (E4), DB is attached to `[]` \u2014 no networks (E5). That directly explains DNS failure in E3. No shared network = no `db` name resolution.\n* DB process itself is fine, so this is dependency-connectivity, not DB crash:\n  * DB `healthy`, `exit_code 0`, `running true` (E5)\n  * DB logs: `database system is ready to accept connections` (E7)\n  * `recent_events` shows `health_status: healthy` with successful `pg_isready` checks (E6).\n  * `recent_events` also shows kill/stop/die/destroy/rename/create/start cycles for both containers at `00:01:47` and `00:02:20-00:02:26` (E6), consistent with recent recreation that left DB without network.\n\n**Storage / uploads path ruled out:**\n\n* `/srv/lab-data`: `use_percent 9.0`, `inode_use_percent 0.2` (E8) \u2014 not full.\n* `/`: `use_percent 6.8`, `inode_use_percent 1.5` (E9) \u2014 not full.\n* `/srv/lab-data/uploads`: `is_dir true`, `owner 1000:1000 mode 0755`, `app 1000:1000 can_write true` (E10).\n* `/srv/lab-data`: same `1000:1000`, `can_write true` (E11).\n* App mount `bind /srv/lab-data -> /data rw true`, `user 1000:1000` (E4) matches writable owners in E10/E11.\n\nSymptom in app (`upload` 500 / `health` 503) is downstream of DB network detachment. Fix requires re-attaching `incidentlab-db-1` to `incidentlab_default` (person approval required) \u2014 no storage fix needed.\n",
